          "annotations": [],
          "text": "It might—depending on what’s being claimed and what evidence is being offered.\n\nA scientific claim should be tied to things like:\n\n- testable predictions  \n- measurable evidence  \n- peer-reviewed studies or reproducible data  \n- clear distinction between established findings and hypotheses  \n- willingness to revise if evidence changes  \n\nSpeculation, by contrast, often relies on “could be,” “might explain,” or “it’s possible” without enough evidence to verify it.\n\nSo a fair way to put it would be: **if the idea is being presented as a possibility, it may be reasonable speculation; if it’s being presented as established fact without strong evidence, then yes, that’s not really science.**",
